# ============================================================================================
# DECLARED VERDICTS for the Lean proof gate — `tools/lean-proof.py`, `make leanproof`.
#
# One row per `#print axioms` honesty gate in the keystone peer's proof track, stating the
# axiom set that declaration MUST report. The run must produce EXACTLY this set of rows —
# no more, no less — which is the same rule the prover tables carry (`PV_EXPECT`,
# `TM_EXPECT`): an undeclared gate is an ungraded gate, and a declared gate that stops
# printing is a proof that stopped being checked.
#
# WHY A TABLE AND NOT `grep -c sorryAx`. Asked D13's question — what does this assert, and
# what else satisfies it? — a grep over the build log is satisfied by a build that printed
# no axiom lines at all, which is exactly what deleting a `#print axioms` line produces.
# That is negative control `neg-ungate`, and it is why the names are declared here rather
# than counted from the output.
#
# THE TRUSTED SET is Lean's three standard axioms: `propext`, `Classical.choice`,
# `Quot.sound`. Nothing else may appear in a row — `tools/lean-proof.py` rejects the FILE
# at parse time if it does. `sorryAx` (an unfinished proof) and any hand-written `axiom`
# are holes, and a gate you can declare your way out of is not a gate. If a proof genuinely
# needs a new axiom, that is a change to `docs/LEAN-SEAM.md`'s verdicts first — the row
# stops being CLOSED — and to this file second.
#
# HOW THIS WAS DERIVED (D15 — a derived number is a claim). The rows below are the output
# of one clean `lake build EntityCoreProofs` against keystone's Lean tree at the revision
# `docs/LEAN-SEAM.md` pins by digest, transcribed unedited. That is a starting point, not a
# justification: the gate's content is that the numbers CANNOT MOVE WITHOUT A DIFF HERE.
# Re-deriving this file to make a red run go green defeats it entirely — the failing run is
# telling you a proof changed, and the ledger rows that cite it need re-reading first.
#
# 40 gates. 25 of them are cited by `docs/LEAN-SEAM.md` (24 discharging + 1 pinned as a
# rejected correspondence); `tools/lean-proof.py` checks that tie separately and reports
# LEDGER_UNCOVERED if a pinned theorem is not among the gates that reported. The other 15
# are the proof track's own — the CBOR float-encoding and canonical-sort proofs, and five
# CapabilityProofs helper lemmas — graded here because the peer gates them, not because
# this repo's models rely on them.
#
# 37 → 40 on 2026-09-06: keystone adopted the §5.5a packet and added a theorem per pattern
# form. The three arrived as `UNDECLARED_GATE` failures from this file's own both-directions
# check, which is the outcome it exists for — three new theorems nobody here had read would
# otherwise have been absorbed silently by a gate that only counted.
#
# Format:
#   gate|<file, relative to protocol-generator/lean>|<full Lean name>|<axioms, or `-`>
#   warn|<substring a warning line must contain>|<why it is tolerated, and who owns it>
# ============================================================================================

# ── proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean — §3.2 CBOR float shortest-form encoding ──────
# Not cited by the seam ledger; no model in this repo abstracts float encoding (ledger row
# O2 declares content encoding BY-DESIGN unowned here). Graded because the peer gates it.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.tryHalf_widens|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.trySingle_widens|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.encode_uses_half|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.encode_uses_single|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.encode_uses_double|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.encode_nan|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/FloatProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Float.Proofs.encode_inf|propext,Quot.sound

# ── proofs/EntityCoreProofs/SortProofs.lean — canonical map-key ordering ────────────────────
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/SortProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Proofs.lexCmp_self|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/SortProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Proofs.keyCmp_self|propext,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/SortProofs.lean|EntityCore.Codec.Proofs.keyLe_refl|propext,Quot.sound

# ── proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean — the authority interior ─────────────────
# This is the file the seam ledger lives on. Ledger rows in brackets below; a name with no
# bracket is a helper the peer gates and no model here cites.
#
# [L5,L6] attenuation composes along a chain — the row that makes Tamarin's `no_escalation`
# a statement about the protocol rather than about a free unary function symbol.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesSeg_trans|propext
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.scopeSubset_trans|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.grantSubset_trans|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.isAttenuated_trans|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L1] the chain verdict is a function of the chain, not of the evaluation time.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.walk_time_stable|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.verifyChain_time_stable|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.verifyChain_time_independent|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L1,L9] a foreign-rooted single-sig chain is denied outright.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.verifyChain_foreign_root|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L4] the §4.10(b) depth brake is pure structure.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.chainExceedsDepth_iff|propext
# [L8] a satisfied multi-sig root means a real quorum, including this peer.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.multiSigRootOk_quorum|propext
# [L11] the walk actually applies the per-edge check — L5 composes the step, L11 takes it.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.walk_allow_cons|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.walk_allow_leaf_attenuated|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.walk_allow_head|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.walk_allow_link_facts|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.edgeOk_atten|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.edgeOk_caveats|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L6] the §5.4 matcher: reflexive, transitive, deny-override, and the 0.8.1 F40 split.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesSeg_refl|propext
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesScope_excl_override|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesScope_id_excl_override|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesIdPattern_literal|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L3] an authority holding no grants covers nothing — deny-by-default at the §5.2 gate.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.checkPermission_no_grants_deny|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L7] §5.5a namespace isolation for the PEER-RELATIVE form; H (`hframed`) is what scopes it
# there, and is false — not merely unproved — for the absolute form. CLOSED as of 2026-09-06,
# when the companion theorem below landed. The gate proves each theorem holds; that the three
# forms between them COVER §5.5a is the ledger's reading, not this file's assertion.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.grantPattern_namespace_isolation|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L7] the absolute NAMED form — the residual this repo routed, adopted 2026-09-06.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.absolutePattern_names_one_peer|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L12] absolute patterns canonicalize identically in any frame — the equation our symbolic
# theories encode as `canon(awild(p), fr) = awild(p)`.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.canonSegs_absolute_frame_independent|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# [L13] the wildcard form is peer-agnostic BY DESIGN. Note the axiom set is `propext` alone,
# not the three-axiom set of its neighbours: a narrower set is still a set that must not move
# silently, which is why this file grades the set rather than the count.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.wildcardPattern_peer_agnostic|propext
# [L3, pinned REJECTED] considered and discharges nothing here — see LEAN-SEAM.md §4.2.
# Still required to be proved: a stale rejection misleads exactly as a stale citation does.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.checkResourceScope_no_targets_deny|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
# Helpers the peer gates; no ledger row cites them.
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.isAttenuated_refl|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.allowed_chain_leaf_atten_root|propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.matchesSeg_head_lit|propext
gate|proofs/EntityCoreProofs/CapabilityProofs.lean|EntityCore.Capability.Proofs.head?_some_cons|propext

# ── DECLARED WARNINGS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# D13: a tool warning is a build failure. Lean reports `sorry` AS a warning, so this gate
# cannot be indifferent to them — but it also cannot go red on day one for a warning that
# belongs to another repo. So: every warning is a failure UNLESS declared here, by exact
# substring, with an owner.
#
# NONE ARE DECLARED, and that is a state this file should be checked against rather than
# assumed. One was: `String.dropRight` deprecated, in keystone's shipping
# `src/EntityCore/Capability.lean`, routed 2026-08-30 with the instruction "delete this row
# when they land it." They landed it 2026-09-06 (`dropRight` → `dropEnd`), so the row is gone
# and the build is warning-clean. Their note is worth keeping because we got it wrong: we
# flagged the `String.Slice` return type as a possible blocker, and it is not one —
# `String.startsWith` is generic over `ForwardPattern`, so the slice is taken with no
# `.toString` copy. They did not stop at typechecking either, since typechecking is not
# equivalence: 21 inputs including 2- and 3-byte multi-byte prefixes, zero divergence.
#
# Keystone disclosed two more of the same class (`String.data`, `String.get` in `Host.lean`)
# and deliberately did NOT bundle them, so the conformance re-measurement stayed unambiguous
# about cause. They are outside the two files this ledger pins, so this gate cannot see them
# — recorded here because "the gate is clean" and "the peer has no deprecations" are
# different claims, and only the first is ours to make.
